@startuml activity-fr-04
' Report §2.1 — FR-04 Adjust a published session's capacity.
' Source: EventController.changeCapacity, UpdateCapacityRequest,
' EventApplicationService.changeSessionCapacity, Event.changeSessionCapacity,
' CatalogEventConsumers.sessionCapacityChanged, SessionViewProjection, SessionView.
!include include/style.iuml
!include include/activity.iuml

title FR-04 — Adjust a session's seat capacity

|Organiser|
start
:PUT /api/v1/events/{id}/sessions/{sessionId}/capacity
{seatCapacity};

|event-catalog-service|
if (seatCapacity <= 0?) then (yes)
  $ERR:400 VALIDATION_FAILED;
  stop
else (no)
endif
:EventApplicationService.changeSessionCapacity;
if (event exists?) then (no)
  $ERR:404 EVENT_NOT_FOUND;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:Event.changeSessionCapacity(sessionId, capacity);
if (session in this event?) then (no)
  $ERR:404 SESSION_NOT_FOUND;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:Session.changeSeatCapacity(new value),
record SessionCapacityChanged;
:EventRepository.save → catalogdb.sessions;
:after commit, StreamBridge sends;

|Kafka|
$EVT:session-capacity-changed
key: sessionId>

fork
  |event-catalog-service|
  $OK:200 OK SessionResponse;
  |Organiser|
  :sees the new capacity;
fork again
  |registration-service|
  :session-capacity-changed<
  :SessionViewProjection.apply
  find or create the SessionView;
  :setCapacity(new value)
  reservedSeats untouched
  → regdb.session_views;
end fork
stop

note right
  <b>Reductions are accepted, never rejected.</b>
  Seats already held or confirmed are kept
  (grandfathered). New registrations are refused
  with 409 SESSION_FULL while reservedSeats +
  quantity would exceed the new capacity (FR-06).
  No processed-event check here: applying the
  same absolute capacity twice is harmless.
end note

note left
  Allowed for DRAFT and PUBLISHED events.
  A CANCELLED event refuses the change,
  but no use case on main cancels an event.
end note
@enduml
